Z||000000||gmata||05-11-2000||10:44 PM||||I'm going to install an aftermarket sunroof.  What is the largest sunroof dimension that I can install? ie. would 15 X 33 work?||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||05-11-2000||11:05 PM||||Welcome to the forum and all that, but WHY would you want to cut in for some leaky aftermarket sunroof? Every junkyard I come across has at least one sunroof fiero. Just swap roof panels and put in a new headliner and badda bing badda boom. You could probably even recover some of your cost seling your plain roof to a kit builder.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||05-11-2000||11:28 PM||||15X33 is too big. The curve of the roof prvents using the large roofs I think the max width is 26". It would be better and a lot bigger just swapping roof panels. Takes about 2 hours to swap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||gmata||05-12-2000||11:50 AM||||I forgot to mentioned that I currently have an aftermarket sunroof, but it is old and I want to replace it.  The only problem is that the width is 15 inches.  Most sunroof installers don't want to install a 15'' sunroof.  I was wondering what the dimensions were on the factory sunroof.  Is the roof modified in anyway when a factory sunroof is installed?  I don't think I want to cut the roof and swap it, so I'm trying to find some other way.  Thanks for you help guys.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||pollock||05-12-2000||03:00 PM||||You don't have to cut the roof at all.  Just remove the panel and swap.<BR>||||reg||1
